   "short": false,
   "hook": "Seoul fever: a record year for visitors",
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Fifteen million foreigners visited Korea in just eight months. A record.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_01.mp3",
     "shot": "screen_full",
     "cam_id": "full",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "open_count"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And they didn't just visit. They caught something.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_02.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "It's called \"Seoul fever.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_03.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "fever"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Hello, world. I'm Master K, and this is the Four Eyes Report.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_04.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Coming up: a fever, a chip boom, a holiday for an alphabet, a very fast country, and why Koreans ask your age.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_05.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Let's start with the fever. Our current affairs correspondent, Ms. Nonfic. She reads the corrections page for fun.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_06.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Good evening. From January to August, fifteen point oh five million foreign visitors came to Korea. A record. That is more people than live in Pennsylvania. Pennsylvania has not commented.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_07.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "vs_penn"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Somebody call Pennsylvania!",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_08.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "August alone: two point two five million. Another record. Much of the growth came from Southeast Asia, thanks to easier entry rules and higher spending.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_09.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "august"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Hello, Singapore, Malaysia, and the Philippines! We see you!",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_10.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "And a new word came with them. \"Seoul fever,\" and its cousin, \"Busan fever.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_11.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "fevers"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Both words describe travelers who miss the city after they go home. In other words: repeat customers.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_12.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "repeat"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I'm a doctor. Not that kind. But I have a diagnosis: it's good for the Seoul.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_13.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Please don't.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_14.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Seoul-searching. Seoul food. Seoul mate. I have a whole list.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_15.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "puns"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "For the record, I heard all of that. Now, rankings. Agoda's booking data for the first half of the year puts Seoul fourth in Asia for repeat visits.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_16.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "rank"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Fourth! Who beat us?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_17.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Tokyo, Bangkok, and Bali. Osaka is fifth.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_18.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "rank"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Fourth place. The saddest number at the Olympics.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_19.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Analysts credit the range: K-content, festivals, food, beauty, shopping, and convenience stores that never close.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_20.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "why"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "So the fever has a cause: a lot going on, and a snack at every hour.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_21.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Symptoms include booking your second trip before the first one ends.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_22.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Treatment: none known.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_23.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  },
