   "short": false,
   "hook": "A holiday for an alphabet: Hangul Day",
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Next, a holiday you might not know: Hangul Day, October ninth. To explain it, our historian, Dr. H.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_56.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "hangul_day"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Dr. H, what does the H stand for?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_57.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "...That's classified.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_58.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Actually, Hangul Day is a public holiday. Korea takes a day off to celebrate its writing system.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_59.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "day_off"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "A holiday for an alphabet? In America, we just get a song.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_60.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The ABC song is not a holiday.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_61.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "It should be. It has a really good tune.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_62.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Before the fourteen-forties, writing in Korea meant Chinese characters, and learning them took years.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_63.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "hanja"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "King Sejong the Great created Hangul in the fourteen-forties so that ordinary people could read and write.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_64.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "sejong",
      "t1446"
     ],
     "screen_split": [
      0.5
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "And here is the secret. The consonants copy the shape your mouth and tongue make when you say them.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_65.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "letters"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "The letters are diagrams? So it's basically the first user-friendly interface.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_66.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Version one. Still no patch notes after five hundred eighty years.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_67.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "patch"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Today it has twenty-four letters: fourteen consonants and ten vowels.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_68.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "twenty4"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Learners say you can learn to read it in a day.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_69.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Let me test that. Write your name.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_70.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Done!",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_71.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "kangfree_name"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "It says \"Kang-peu-ri.\" Close enough.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_72.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "category": "current_affairs",
   "desk": "IS THIS NORMAL?",
   "headline": "Is this normal in Korea? Ppalli-ppalli",
   "characters": {
    "panel": {
     "head": "../../cast/kangfree_head.png",
     "body": "../../cast/kangfree_body.png",
