   "short": false,
   "hook": "Why Koreans ask your age",
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Last topic. A question every foreigner hears within five minutes.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_82.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "\"How old are you?\"",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_83.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "how_old"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "In Korea, that's grammar.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_84.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Korean has speech levels. To pick the right one, you need to know who is older. So the question is not nosy. It is a setting.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_85.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "levels"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Until 2023, Korea also had \"Korean age\": you are one at birth, and everyone gets a year older every January first. A baby born on December thirty-first turns two the next day.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_86.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "kage"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Two days old and already two!",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_87.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "In June 2023, Korea switched official documents to international age. Everyone became one or two years younger.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_88.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "june23"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Korea invented the cheapest anti-aging treatment in history: legislation.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_89.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "anti"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Social life did not change. People still ask.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_90.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "One more thing. Koreans say \"our.\" Our mom, our house, our school. Even \"our wife.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_91.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "our"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "\"Our\" signals belonging, not ownership. It means: we share this.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_92.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So he's not sharing his wife. He's sharing the word.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_93.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Please don't say that in English.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep03_94.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    }
   ]
  },
